WEBVTT

00:13.930 --> 00:17.600
My knight. This path is different
from the one we took to get here.

00:18.435 --> 00:20.353
Because we've received our next order.

00:21.563 --> 00:24.107
Heroes don't have a fixed path.

00:32.991 --> 00:35.535
There are more people on the road now.

00:35.618 --> 00:37.370
That's because where we're going next...

00:37.454 --> 00:40.165
is organizing a small festival...

00:41.458 --> 00:44.085
- By the way, Xylo...
- Yeah?

00:44.919 --> 00:49.674
Isn't it about time we take a break...?

00:50.592 --> 00:52.093
Didn't we just take a break?

00:52.177 --> 00:55.055
I can't... go on...

01:02.312 --> 01:04.230
Is that our destination?

01:04.314 --> 01:05.815
Yes...

01:05.899 --> 01:08.109
It's an important fortress
that serves as a defense point

01:08.193 --> 01:10.320
for the Second Capital.

01:10.945 --> 01:14.407
A natural fortress guarded
by a great river and cliffs,

01:17.077 --> 01:18.369
Mureed Fortress,

01:18.870 --> 01:21.498
also known as "the Wayfarer's Nest."

01:25.710 --> 01:26.795
It's cheap!

01:26.878 --> 01:28.463
All the items here are fresh!

01:28.546 --> 01:30.590
Young man, you have good taste.

01:33.343 --> 01:35.970
Oh no, I don't have enough military scrip.

01:36.054 --> 01:37.972
Can I have five of these?

01:38.556 --> 01:41.351
Does anyone want to send a letter?

01:41.434 --> 01:43.436
- Please send this to my mother.
- We can send it anywhere

01:43.520 --> 01:45.021
in the Federated Kingdom!

01:46.731 --> 01:47.857
Hey.

01:49.400 --> 01:52.112
You're like this as soon
as you get back from the repair shop?

01:52.695 --> 01:54.781
Dotta, you never learn, do you?

01:54.864 --> 01:56.616
It's fine, it's fine.

01:56.699 --> 01:58.827
A little stealing won't hurt.

01:58.910 --> 02:00.245
It's a festival, after all.

02:00.328 --> 02:02.789
Even if it's the long-awaited
Great Exchange,

02:02.872 --> 02:04.833
it'll be bad if you get caught.

02:04.916 --> 02:07.794
The merchants of Verkle Development
Corporation really love money.

02:10.547 --> 02:12.924
Come on, don't be so stiff.

02:13.007 --> 02:15.385
Let's enjoy our rare day off.

02:16.678 --> 02:19.973
Heroes like us don't have
the concept of a day off.

02:20.056 --> 02:23.476
Right now, we're just on standby at best.

02:23.560 --> 02:29.566
But we can at least get some time
that could be called a break.

02:30.692 --> 02:32.068
Oh, yeah.

02:32.152 --> 02:36.156
That's all Venetim ever says.

02:40.493 --> 02:43.830
It would be even better
if there were girls...

02:44.455 --> 02:46.082
Forget it.

02:46.166 --> 02:48.501
Even if there was a place like that,

02:48.585 --> 02:50.837
they wouldn't allow us to go.

02:51.337 --> 02:52.881
You're right...

02:55.717 --> 02:57.927
Commander in chief, where are you?

02:58.511 --> 03:00.638
- Commander in Chief Xylo!
- What?

03:00.722 --> 03:02.515
Commander in Chief Xylo.

03:02.599 --> 03:04.601
The caravan traders are here.

03:04.684 --> 03:06.603
Go and buy me some wine.

03:06.686 --> 03:10.315
Unfortunately,
our national treasury is empty.

03:10.398 --> 03:13.776
Have you forgotten that
we're out of military scrip?

03:14.360 --> 03:17.739
If you want wine,
borrow money to buy some.

03:17.822 --> 03:19.908
Aren't Venetim and the others
free right now?

03:19.991 --> 03:23.536
The chancellor is keeping an eye
on sticky-fingered Dotta.

03:23.620 --> 03:25.538
He's bluffing again.

03:25.622 --> 03:29.167
Where's Tsav? Hasn't he returned
from his mission yet?

03:29.250 --> 03:31.419
Yes, he's on loan from another unit.

03:32.754 --> 03:36.841
Everyone's like that.
They have no respect for the king!

03:36.925 --> 03:40.428
Seriously, can't you just
let me read in peace?

03:43.598 --> 03:46.434
There you are, my knight!

03:47.018 --> 03:48.728
One leaves, and another comes...

03:49.395 --> 03:50.897
Your door was open.

03:50.980 --> 03:53.191
Aren't you being too careless?

03:53.274 --> 03:55.735
Dotta let himself out.

03:55.818 --> 03:57.362
He has the key.

03:57.445 --> 04:00.114
My knight, aren't you visiting
the Great Exchange?

04:00.198 --> 04:01.950
I don't want to see those Holy Knights.

04:02.033 --> 04:05.286
Then get up and play with me!

04:05.370 --> 04:06.746
Why?

04:06.829 --> 04:08.623
Why don't you go by yourself?

04:08.706 --> 04:12.293
I... I am a goddess.

04:12.377 --> 04:14.879
I am not interested in that.

04:16.256 --> 04:18.675
You don't like being watched
by Holy Knights?

04:19.676 --> 04:22.220
Don't say things like that.

04:22.303 --> 04:23.221
More importantly,

04:23.304 --> 04:26.683
I will grant you the honor
of playing with me.

04:26.766 --> 04:28.142
Doesn't that make you happy?

04:28.810 --> 04:29.852
Zigg, huh...

04:29.936 --> 04:32.939
Venetim taught me how to play.

04:33.022 --> 04:35.650
It will not be easy to beat me.

04:36.693 --> 04:42.407
This is the orthodox "hidden spear" tactic
once used by the Mayte Kingdom--

04:42.490 --> 04:43.783
Forget it.

04:44.450 --> 04:47.829
If Venetim told you that,
chances are he tricked you.

04:47.912 --> 04:49.080
Huh?

04:50.707 --> 04:52.834
Anyway, I'm busy now.

04:52.917 --> 04:54.919
Huh? You want to read a book?

04:55.003 --> 04:57.380
You can do that later.

04:57.463 --> 04:59.465
I just happened to make a bookmark.

04:59.549 --> 05:01.467
I don't care. You can use it.

05:04.220 --> 05:05.263
By the way,

05:06.055 --> 05:08.808
I am surprised that Xylo likes to read.

05:08.891 --> 05:10.893
- What are you reading?
- Poems.

05:11.394 --> 05:12.812
Poems.

05:14.397 --> 05:15.982
Xylo...

05:16.065 --> 05:17.567
You read poems...

05:17.650 --> 05:19.777
Hey, why are you so surprised?

05:19.861 --> 05:21.904
What kind of poetry collection is it?

05:21.988 --> 05:24.699
I will grant you the honor
of reading it to me.

05:24.782 --> 05:25.742
I refuse.

05:26.576 --> 05:29.620
Then we can read it together, at least.

05:29.704 --> 05:30.913
That's okay, right?

05:32.206 --> 05:35.460
This isn't something a goddess would like.

05:36.210 --> 05:39.422
It's an ancient book of poetry
called "Dragon-Drunk."

05:39.505 --> 05:43.885
It was written by an alcoholic poet
named Altoyard Comette.

05:43.968 --> 05:46.846
In his later years, he began
to fantasize about becoming a dragon.

05:46.929 --> 05:49.891
He practiced flying every night
and ended up killing himself.

05:51.642 --> 05:53.352
He is quite a strange one.

05:53.436 --> 05:56.564
Most poets from that era were like him.

05:57.190 --> 06:00.777
If I hadn't joined the army,
I might have aimed to be a poet like him.

06:00.860 --> 06:02.028
A poet?!

06:02.111 --> 06:04.197
What's wrong? Why are you so startled...

06:04.280 --> 06:05.990
Xylo Forbartz.

06:06.074 --> 06:07.909
So this is where you were.

06:08.409 --> 06:10.912
I didn't expect Lady Teoritta
to be with you too.

06:10.995 --> 06:15.500
Kivia, I did not expect you
to come either.

06:16.709 --> 06:19.504
Didn't expect the noble Commander
of the Holy Knights

06:19.587 --> 06:21.255
to come all the way here.

06:21.339 --> 06:23.841
Has our fate finally been decided?

06:24.926 --> 06:27.136
Or is there another operation order?

06:27.220 --> 06:29.597
Both.

06:29.680 --> 06:32.100
But I'm here about something else.

06:32.767 --> 06:34.393
There's something I want
to discuss with you.

06:34.477 --> 06:35.561
Well, I don't have anything to say.

06:37.021 --> 06:38.523
Come with me. I'll go get...

06:38.606 --> 06:40.024
I will go too!

06:40.566 --> 06:41.734
What?

06:42.318 --> 06:44.695
The Great Exchange festival
is happening in town right now.

06:44.779 --> 06:47.698
I think it is a good idea
to talk while shopping.

06:47.782 --> 06:52.161
If Kivia is around, then a goddess
like me can go too, right?

06:52.245 --> 06:54.872
Yes, what a splendid idea.

06:54.956 --> 06:57.792
All right. Let's go, my knight!

07:09.470 --> 07:10.388
Good grief...

07:10.471 --> 07:11.931
- Xylo, look!
- What?

07:12.515 --> 07:14.142
Is that food?

07:14.225 --> 07:16.394
Or is it some kind of accessory?

07:16.477 --> 07:18.104
It's candy.

07:18.187 --> 07:19.689
You've never seen it before?

07:19.772 --> 07:21.607
Can... dy...?

07:21.691 --> 07:25.153
It did not exist in the era
when I was created.

07:25.236 --> 07:27.572
They are just like jewels.

07:27.655 --> 07:28.739
Huh?

07:30.700 --> 07:32.493
What is that long, thin food?

07:32.577 --> 07:33.411
Hm?

07:33.494 --> 07:34.829
It's fried noodles.

07:35.329 --> 07:36.956
It's a Western dish
in which long, thin wheat strips

07:37.039 --> 07:38.624
are stir-fried with fermented sauce
and butter...

07:38.708 --> 07:41.461
Wow, I see! Then what about that?

07:42.336 --> 07:44.172
Look, the one with the bear sign!

07:45.006 --> 07:46.215
That...

07:46.716 --> 07:48.759
What is that? I've never seen it before.

07:48.843 --> 07:50.595
Miwoolies Creams.

07:50.678 --> 07:52.722
It's a popular ice cream
in the First Capital.

07:52.805 --> 07:55.600
Whipped cream is poured over shaved ice,

07:55.683 --> 07:57.310
then topped with honey and nuts.

07:57.393 --> 07:58.561
It's absolutely divine.

07:58.644 --> 08:00.438
And that bear is a mascot.

08:00.521 --> 08:02.565
They're currently looking
for a name for it.

08:03.107 --> 08:05.151
How wonderful!

08:05.234 --> 08:06.986
I can feel the progress of civilization.

08:07.069 --> 08:08.738
That's the first time I've heard of it.

08:09.739 --> 08:10.698
How do you know so much about it?

08:10.781 --> 08:13.993
It's not surprising.
I eat frozen treats like this too.

08:16.537 --> 08:19.457
What were you thinking just now?

08:19.540 --> 08:20.791
My knight.

08:20.875 --> 08:22.668
That looks good, Xylo.

08:22.752 --> 08:24.587
It looks really delicious.

08:24.670 --> 08:28.049
What do you think?
Don't you want to try it?

08:29.634 --> 08:31.135
I guess I have no choice.

08:31.219 --> 08:33.095
In that case, I'll buy two
of the delicious-looking...

08:33.721 --> 08:35.056
No, make it three.

08:37.433 --> 08:39.018
I'll pass.

08:39.101 --> 08:41.020
I want to keep my military scrip
and not waste it.

08:41.729 --> 08:43.731
You heard her. Two, then.

08:44.690 --> 08:45.566
Go buy them.

08:45.650 --> 08:46.651
I understand.

08:46.734 --> 08:49.320
You can count on me!

08:56.827 --> 08:57.912
Xylo.

08:57.995 --> 09:02.083
- I've changed my opinion of you a little.
- What?

09:04.210 --> 09:07.672
You saved my soldiers in Couveunge

09:08.464 --> 09:12.385
and also saved the civilians we were
about to abandon at Zewan Gan.

09:13.010 --> 09:17.181
The people you saved are thanking you too.

09:18.057 --> 09:19.225
I see.

09:20.977 --> 09:22.645
That's worth something, then.

09:24.897 --> 09:27.775
I didn't know you could smile like that.

09:29.193 --> 09:31.904
After all, too many things
in this world piss me off.

09:32.655 --> 09:36.701
Anyway, you've shown some results.

09:37.910 --> 09:43.916
And Lady Teoritta may have been saved
because she formed a covenant with you.

09:44.000 --> 09:45.459
What do you mean?

09:46.961 --> 09:51.632
Lady Teoritta's existence was confirmed
in the northern ruins.

09:52.425 --> 09:55.011
We, the Thirteenth Order
of the Holy Knights,

09:55.094 --> 09:57.597
were sent to form a covenant
after the excavation

09:57.680 --> 10:00.016
and to manage and utilize her.

10:00.099 --> 10:03.102
But the military and the Temple
were at odds.

10:04.186 --> 10:05.479
That must've been hard on you.

10:06.063 --> 10:07.023
What are you talking about?

10:07.106 --> 10:09.775
It's all because you killed
Goddess Senerva!

10:09.859 --> 10:10.693
What?

10:11.360 --> 10:15.489
After that incident,
the military came up with an idea.

10:15.990 --> 10:18.826
If a goddess could be killed,

10:19.952 --> 10:22.872
could they do the opposite
and increase the number of goddesses?

10:23.914 --> 10:28.544
So the military hoped
to analyze Lady Teoritta.

10:30.630 --> 10:32.506
"Analyze" is just a nice way of saying it.

10:32.590 --> 10:34.925
It's actually a dissection, right?

10:35.009 --> 10:35.843
Of course.

10:36.427 --> 10:41.265
The Temple opposed it,
but the military had the upper hand.

10:41.891 --> 10:45.394
However, the situation
is gradually changing.

10:45.478 --> 10:49.231
You defeated two Demon Blights
in a short period of time

10:49.315 --> 10:51.525
and demonstrated
Lady Teoritta's usefulness.

10:52.902 --> 10:54.945
Demonstrated her usefulness...

10:55.029 --> 10:57.490
Does that mean you thought
she was useless?

10:58.282 --> 11:00.409
She was just discovered,
so her capabilities aren't clear yet...

11:01.160 --> 11:03.913
We know she has the power
to summon swords.

11:03.996 --> 11:06.666
That's what's recorded in the ruins.

11:09.085 --> 11:10.670
It's said that goddesses
descended upon this world

11:10.753 --> 11:13.089
during the First War of Subjugation,

11:13.172 --> 11:16.050
in an age known
as the Great Civilized Era.

11:16.967 --> 11:19.345
Goddesses are a type of "gate."

11:19.428 --> 11:22.181
Their natures vary.

11:24.100 --> 11:26.018
Some can produce potent poisons,

11:26.685 --> 11:29.021
summon lightning strikes
or violent storms,

11:29.605 --> 11:31.482
or see visions of the future.

11:32.817 --> 11:35.528
They awaken with the emergence
of a Demon Blight.

11:35.611 --> 11:39.115
After fulfilling their mission,
they return to their coffins to sleep.

11:41.617 --> 11:44.995
I know about the goddess's abilities.

11:45.079 --> 11:49.959
I even heard that Tatsuya was summoned
from another world by a goddess.

11:50.543 --> 11:53.963
Compared to
the twelve goddesses found so far,

11:54.046 --> 11:57.925
the military believes
her sword-summoning ability is inferior.

11:59.260 --> 12:04.432
So we...
despite knowing what awaits Lady Teoritta...

12:06.892 --> 12:09.603
I see. So that's why you...

12:10.271 --> 12:15.109
Was the suicidal tactic you used
in Couveunge some form of atonement?

12:17.153 --> 12:21.365
So what if a goddess is useless...

12:21.866 --> 12:23.617
Here you go. Thanks for waiting.

12:23.701 --> 12:25.411
Thank you.

12:26.203 --> 12:29.373
Xylo, I got them!
I ended up buying one for Kivia.

12:33.210 --> 12:34.920
Let's all eat together...

12:40.885 --> 12:42.761
Tell me about the next mission.

12:42.845 --> 12:43.721
What?

12:43.804 --> 12:47.766
If I do a good job on the mission,
she won't be dissected, right?

12:49.810 --> 12:54.940
I'll make those Galtuile bastards
acknowledge her usefulness.

12:59.361 --> 13:00.446
It's a defense mission.

13:02.239 --> 13:06.535
You heroes will be the only ones
defending this fortress.

13:07.578 --> 13:08.662
Defend it with your lives.

13:11.040 --> 13:12.958
Defend it with our lives, you say?

13:13.042 --> 13:14.460
That's right.

13:14.543 --> 13:19.173
This fortress will be defended only
by you heroes against the Demon Blight.

13:19.256 --> 13:21.717
In other words, you want us to die?

13:21.800 --> 13:24.220
Xylo, please calm down.

13:24.303 --> 13:25.638
You can't just charge in
and punch or kill--

13:25.721 --> 13:28.057
- Who do you think I am?
- Eek!

13:28.140 --> 13:31.227
Excuse me, but when you say
"defend the fortress with our lives",

13:31.310 --> 13:33.729
what exactly is our objective?

13:35.439 --> 13:38.067
Stay in this fortress. It's that simple.

13:38.150 --> 13:39.818
A battle of attrition, huh?

13:39.902 --> 13:41.946
How long do we have to hold out?

13:42.029 --> 13:43.489
Until you die.

13:45.491 --> 13:48.619
The Ninth and Thirteenth Orders
of the Holy Knights

13:48.702 --> 13:50.955
will hold their strength
in reserve at the rear.

13:51.038 --> 13:53.874
Once you've been annihilated
and the fortress has fallen,

13:53.958 --> 13:56.168
we'll launch a special attack.

13:56.919 --> 13:58.671
The so-called special attack is...

13:58.754 --> 14:00.130
It's poison.

14:00.214 --> 14:03.842
The Ninth Order's goddess
will perform a miracle.

14:05.302 --> 14:07.429
Will that be enough
to kill the Demon Lord?

14:07.513 --> 14:09.890
I heard that no matter how large
a strike operation is launched,

14:09.974 --> 14:12.893
it can't be completely eliminated, right?

14:12.977 --> 14:14.311
That's right.

14:14.395 --> 14:16.772
The last operation involved sniping

14:16.855 --> 14:19.316
a lethal toxin produced
by the goddess into the target.

14:19.400 --> 14:21.569
In the end, it just temporarily put it
in a state of suspended animation.

14:21.652 --> 14:23.529
Attacking it was pointless.

14:24.071 --> 14:26.991
Even Tsav couldn't finish it off.

14:27.074 --> 14:28.450
Based on this result

14:28.534 --> 14:31.495
and the third goddess's ability
to foresee the future,

14:31.579 --> 14:34.206
Galtuile revised our strategy.

14:34.290 --> 14:38.586
We decided to turn Mureed Fortress
into a giant, lethal poison trap.

14:38.669 --> 14:42.131
To continuously kill this Demon Lord.

14:42.631 --> 14:46.552
Will this even surpass
his amazing regeneration ability?

14:46.635 --> 14:49.763
And you want us to buy time here
until we die for that?

14:49.847 --> 14:51.056
That's right.

14:51.140 --> 14:52.933
We're going to make Mureed Fortress

14:53.017 --> 14:56.437
the tombstone
of Demon Blight Number Fifteen, Iblis.

14:56.520 --> 14:59.023
Um... Commander.

14:59.106 --> 15:04.486
Why can't we escape after successfully
luring the Demon Lord in?

15:04.570 --> 15:07.156
It's Galtuile's decision.

15:07.239 --> 15:10.367
If even one of you leaves the fortress,

15:10.451 --> 15:13.787
the sacred seal on your neck
will kill everyone in your unit.

15:14.914 --> 15:17.166
Everyone in the unit?

15:17.249 --> 15:19.168
Why go to such lengths?

15:19.251 --> 15:21.879
Will we cause trouble if we live?

15:29.637 --> 15:31.430
I guess they really don't like us.

15:31.513 --> 15:33.766
Understood. We'll carry out the operation.

15:33.849 --> 15:34.725
What--

15:34.808 --> 15:38.646
However, there are a few points
of the operation I'd like to improve.

15:38.729 --> 15:39.688
Improve?

15:39.772 --> 15:45.194
First, the rule that if one of us leaves
the fortress, all of us will die.

15:45.736 --> 15:47.655
That's actually pretty bad.

15:47.738 --> 15:48.656
Why?

15:48.739 --> 15:53.077
We're a group of criminals
with flawed personalities.

15:53.160 --> 15:57.706
I'm sure someone will want to leave
the fortress and end it quickly.

15:57.790 --> 15:59.583
If that happens,
this operation will be ruined.

15:59.667 --> 16:00.501
So,

16:01.126 --> 16:02.628
it shouldn't be that if one person leaves,

16:02.711 --> 16:06.256
but if everyone escapes, then we all die.

16:06.340 --> 16:10.427
I believe that way, the operation
can be carried out more reliably.

16:10.511 --> 16:11.971
Oh, and one more thing.

16:12.054 --> 16:13.931
Regarding Lady Teoritta,

16:15.057 --> 16:19.311
our goddess has strong compassion.

16:19.395 --> 16:22.815
Even if those around her object,
she'll likely choose to stay.

16:22.898 --> 16:24.441
Please allow that as well.

16:24.525 --> 16:27.695
I... I'm in no position
to give such permission.

16:27.778 --> 16:29.071
By military order, the goddess

16:29.154 --> 16:31.031
is under the Thirteenth Order
of the Holy Knights' jurisdiction--

16:31.115 --> 16:35.160
Xylo.
Please contact Commander Kivia at once.

16:35.244 --> 16:36.370
Got it.

16:40.124 --> 16:42.126
Is there anything else you want?

16:42.209 --> 16:44.545
Troops. We don't have enough people.

16:44.628 --> 16:46.839
Understood. What else?

16:46.922 --> 16:47.923
Weapons and provisions.

16:48.007 --> 16:49.591
Understood. What else?

16:49.675 --> 16:50.509
Amnesty.

16:50.592 --> 16:52.886
Understood. What else?

16:54.722 --> 16:56.223
Amnesty was a joke.

16:56.974 --> 16:58.934
If possible,
I'd like cavalry and artillery.

16:59.476 --> 17:01.478
Is there any way to get
Jayce and Rhyno back?

17:01.562 --> 17:04.106
They're on the Western Front right now.

17:04.189 --> 17:06.316
Tsav, though, can likely be recalled.

17:07.109 --> 17:08.152
Tsav, huh?

17:08.235 --> 17:10.738
Hey, what are you whispering about?

17:10.821 --> 17:12.656
Oh, come on, Xylo.

17:12.740 --> 17:15.451
Isn't Commander Kivia's room that way?

17:15.534 --> 17:16.618
Y-You're right.

17:16.702 --> 17:19.580
Leave it to me. I'll make it happen.

17:19.663 --> 17:21.498
Trust me.

17:21.582 --> 17:23.625
I don't trust you at all.

17:23.709 --> 17:25.085
Can you really do it?

17:26.128 --> 17:27.629
Well, how do I put this?

17:27.713 --> 17:30.090
No one believes me,

17:30.758 --> 17:32.426
but you know what?

17:33.343 --> 17:34.678
Despite how I look,

17:34.762 --> 17:38.474
I'm a man who's one step away
from saving the world.

17:44.354 --> 17:47.232
This place is quite gloomy.

17:47.316 --> 17:50.694
Shouldn't you be taking me
to the tribunal?

17:50.778 --> 17:54.364
My apologies, Venetim Leopool.

17:54.448 --> 17:57.993
I had hoped to speak with you
in a more formal room.

17:58.077 --> 18:01.038
I've always wanted to meet you.

18:01.121 --> 18:02.873
I've even respected you.

18:02.956 --> 18:04.583
Respect?

18:04.666 --> 18:07.586
Do you also want to make
a living by conning people?

18:07.669 --> 18:11.298
If that's the case,
you shouldn't respect someone like me.

18:11.381 --> 18:13.425
After all, I got caught in the end.

18:13.509 --> 18:16.929
That's right. You're absolutely right.

18:17.012 --> 18:19.932
If I were to talk
about the crimes I committed,

18:20.015 --> 18:21.433
the most serious would be

18:21.517 --> 18:24.645
the attempted sale
of the palace to a circus...

18:25.646 --> 18:28.107
That was an unprecedented crime.

18:28.190 --> 18:32.694
In order to sell the capital's land
to a circus performing in the capital,

18:32.778 --> 18:35.531
you fabricated
the capital relocation plan.

18:35.614 --> 18:37.116
That's impressive.

18:37.199 --> 18:41.328
Actually, I was going to take
the down payment and leave.

18:42.162 --> 18:43.914
There's also investment fraud,

18:43.997 --> 18:47.000
counterfeiting antiques
and lottery tickets.

18:47.084 --> 18:51.046
The Verkle Development Corporation
sued you for over 100 crimes.

18:51.130 --> 18:53.632
I'm sorry. I've been reflecting on it.

18:53.715 --> 18:55.884
There's no need for that.

18:55.968 --> 18:57.386
Rather,

18:57.469 --> 19:00.514
why did you want to be a con artist?

19:01.306 --> 19:07.062
To be honest, ever since I was a kid,
I've hated seeing people disappointed.

19:07.146 --> 19:09.690
So I'd make up a lie to placate them

19:09.773 --> 19:12.234
and tell them what they wanted to hear.

19:12.317 --> 19:14.945
That's a truly remarkable effort.

19:15.028 --> 19:19.449
I can't believe you came up with
such a grand plan to please everyone.

19:19.533 --> 19:21.493
Yes...

19:21.577 --> 19:22.828
Excuse me...

19:22.911 --> 19:25.414
Will I be sentenced to death?

19:25.497 --> 19:28.125
No, unfortunately not.

19:28.625 --> 19:32.254
Actually, you won't be
sentenced for fraud.

19:32.337 --> 19:36.466
- Not fraud? Then...
- The big problem is this.

19:37.342 --> 19:41.180
This is the third-rate newspaper
I used to work for.

19:41.263 --> 19:42.681
What about this article?

19:42.764 --> 19:44.933
You wrote this article.

19:45.017 --> 19:49.479
It says that in the Temple, Galtuile,
and even among the royals,

19:49.563 --> 19:52.441
there are spies influenced
by the Demon Blight,

19:52.524 --> 19:55.652
hiding in human form.

19:56.153 --> 19:58.989
Ah... I did write that.

19:59.072 --> 20:02.284
Because there were no new scandals
involving the Holy Knights and goddesses,

20:02.367 --> 20:03.869
nor any new royal controversies,

20:03.952 --> 20:05.954
my superiors told me to write articles

20:06.038 --> 20:08.582
that would stir up
the people's anxiety even more.

20:09.875 --> 20:11.668
I'll be honest with you.

20:11.752 --> 20:16.715
Fraud, fabrication, writing scandals,
or even conspiracy theories,

20:16.798 --> 20:18.383
do whatever you want.

20:19.301 --> 20:20.510
However,

20:21.136 --> 20:23.764
writing the truth is quite troublesome.

20:24.640 --> 20:25.515
Huh?

20:25.599 --> 20:28.101
Especially since you have the ability

20:28.185 --> 20:30.437
to make people believe
your fabricated content.

20:30.938 --> 20:34.983
Or at least, the ability
to make us believe it.

20:35.067 --> 20:41.865
- Huh? Ah, no... Please wait! I...
- To prevent you from telling the truth,

20:41.949 --> 20:45.369
we'll put a special shackle
on your sacred seal.

20:47.454 --> 20:49.248
Huh? Wait...

20:49.915 --> 20:51.750
- Please... Please wait!
- Unfortunately,

20:51.833 --> 20:54.294
the death penalty is too good for you.

20:54.378 --> 20:56.255
H-How could this be?

20:56.922 --> 20:59.508
I don't know anything.

21:00.259 --> 21:03.929
I just didn't want to disappoint anyone...

21:05.430 --> 21:07.933
Venetim Leopool.

21:08.809 --> 21:10.143
I am sentencing you

21:11.103 --> 21:13.146
to be a hero.

21:16.942 --> 21:21.071
I can't believe he agreed to
everything except the amnesty.

21:21.154 --> 21:26.660
If the goddess is in danger,
it's Venetim's job to get her out, right?

21:26.743 --> 21:29.037
He really knows
how to take advantage of things.

21:29.121 --> 21:33.041
That guy is sure to be killed in the chaos
on the battlefield someday.

21:34.084 --> 21:37.379
By the way,
Tsav has returned to the unit, right?

21:37.462 --> 21:38.922
Probably.

21:40.799 --> 21:44.344
Maybe I'd be better off
staying with Venetim.

21:44.428 --> 21:48.140
Feels like Tsav's going to cause
trouble any minute now...

21:49.016 --> 21:50.267
Again?

21:50.350 --> 21:52.227
Hey, hey, he's so lucky.

21:52.311 --> 21:54.229
This is the seventh time.

21:54.313 --> 21:55.272
Heh.

21:58.483 --> 22:00.360
It's another big win.

22:01.611 --> 22:03.322
I'll take it.

22:03.405 --> 22:06.199
Alright, hand over
the military scrip you raised.

22:06.283 --> 22:09.411
Ugh, how could you do that?

22:09.494 --> 22:10.370
What?

22:10.454 --> 22:12.039
You got a problem with that?

22:12.122 --> 22:16.335
No. Actually, my eyesight
and hearing are incredibly sharp.

22:16.418 --> 22:18.962
You see, I'm a man
with a strong sense of justice.

22:19.046 --> 22:21.423
I can't stand it
when people do bad things.

22:22.007 --> 22:24.217
If you put down the military scrip
and leave now,

22:24.301 --> 22:25.427
I won't give you a hard time--

22:25.510 --> 22:30.682
You jerk, that's enough!
If you say something like that again...

22:36.813 --> 22:39.024
You don't need it anymore, right?

22:39.900 --> 22:42.527
That naughty hand you use to cheat.

22:45.447 --> 22:49.242
Honestly... That's why I said that...

22:50.619 --> 22:52.079
But then again,

22:58.168 --> 22:59.795
I'm hungry.
